course: dictionary
lesson: 5375
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning is right. Knead is one of these words. «She kneaded the dough with floury hands» is about bread, because dough is something you cook.
explain: Now read «Kittens knead their mother's tummy to make her milk flow.» There is no dough and no bread here. Kittens, tummy and milk are the clues, so this knead is about a cat pushing its paws, not about cooking. Always ask: what word would fit here?
explain: Then test your meaning in the sentence. Knead means to press, fold and stretch with your hands, or to press and rub muscles. Put that meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Knead» means to press, fold and stretch dough with your hands to make bread.
fact: «Knead» also means to press and rub muscles, like in a massage.
fact: Cats «knead» by pushing their paws in and out on something soft, like a blanket.
fact: When dough is kneaded, it becomes stretchy, so the bread can rise.
fact: Clues such as dough, muscles, blanket or kittens tell you which meaning of knead is right.
exercise: «She kneaded the dough until it felt smooth.» What does knead mean here? | To sing softly while you work | *To press, fold and stretch dough with your hands | Bake in the oven | To cut into small pieces
exercise: Which word in «Kittens knead their mother's tummy to make her milk flow» shows that knead is not about bread? | Milk | Flow | *Kittens | Tummy
exercise: A physio says, «I will knead your sore shoulders.» What does knead mean? | To hide something under a cloth | *To press and rub muscles, like a massage | To bounce a ball | To stir soup in a pan
test: «The cat began to knead the blanket before settling down to sleep.» What does knead mean here? | To wash the blanket | To tear the blanket up | To fold the blanket neatly | *To push its paws in and out on something soft
test: Ava says knead is only about bread. What clue in the lesson shows she is wrong? | Dough is made from flour | Hands are used for cooking | *Cats knead by pushing their paws in and out on something soft | Bread is cooked in an oven
exam: Mum says she will knead her tired shoulders after work. What does knead mean in this sentence? | To cook a meal | To knock on a door | *To press and rub muscles, like a massage | To stretch a rubber band
